{"chunk_id": "e267550c80c8", "text": "After Bhishma\u2019s fall in the Kurukshetra war, the Kaurava army sinks into despair and calls desperately for Karna, their long\u2011withheld champion. Sanjaya recounts how Karna had refused to fight while Bhishma commanded, angered after being publicly classified by Bhishma as only an \u201cArdha\u2011ratha.\u201d With Bhishma gone, the Kauravas now look to Karna as their last great hope, like men seeking a boat to cross a dangerous river. Dhritarashtra anxiously wonders whether Karna can fill the immense void left by Bhishma. When Karna arrives, he mourns Bhishma\u2019s greatness, reflects on the transience of life and power, and then steels himself to defend the Kuru host. Accepting the burden of leadership, he vows to confront the Pandavas and win immortal fame or die in battle.\nAfter Bhishma\u2019s fall, Karna enters the battlefield, mourns him, and vows to defend the Kaurava army and confront the Pandavas.\nThemes: aftermath of Bhishma's fall, Karna's resolve, impermanence of life, loyalty to Duryodhana, war leadership", "vector": [0.0012952015968039632, -0.02287663333117962, 0.00025422172620892525, 0.011458255350589752, -0.014143369160592556, 0.02871210128068924, -0.021627124398946762, -0.0044497111812233925, -0.036395248025655746, -0.002397659933194518, 0.015419462695717812, 0.0045327902771532536, 0.016775311902165413, 0.015618851408362389, -0.0018161069601774216, -0.017386773601174355, 0.042509861290454865, -0.010049236007034779, 0.02863234654068947, -0.04046279564499855, -0.01282739732414484, -0.017479822039604187, -0.0029110880568623543, 0.021560661494731903, -0.03820304572582245, 0.019473716616630554, 0.019992129877209663, -0.02521613799035549, 0.0038482192903757095, -0.021959440782666206, 0.0014405898982658982, -0.006613088306039572, -0.013013494201004505, -0.00833448488265276, -0.028845028951764107, 0.013099896721541882, -0.01439592894166708, -0.019247742369771004, 0.019792741164565086, -0.01103289145976305, 0.0